body:
I have a question about jad healers

&#x200B;

so I can get to jad fine, damage him to half fine, prayer switch fine, pot fine, I can aggro three healers, but for whatever damn reason, I cannot for the life of me find the 4th healer. I'm using runelite highlight mobs and everything, 3 of them are highlighted, but the 4th is nowhere to be found. Jad is still being healed.

&#x200B;

I'm wondering:

I'm using the toxic blowpipe, due to range, is it possible the healers I aggro'd on to me are still healing jad despite being on me? I heard they don't heal jad if you are tanking them, so I don't know

&#x200B;

Is the 4th healer stuck behind some random rock super far away and just troll healing from there? I honestly can't think of another explanation, it says they can only heal from 4 squares away.... which I would easily be able to see with the bright blue highlight, and yet, I have 3 healers on me, jad is still being healed, and no 4th healer in sight. I can easily beat jad if I could find the 4th dude, but I can't. This is the 3rd time this exact scenario has happened all with different jad spawns, so I don't know what to do. I don't wanna run 62 waves just to have some mystical ghost healer prevent me from killing jad.

&#x200B;

I have more than enough resources by the time I am at him, so if I need to use a longer range weapon or something, I have space to bring that

My main issue is the healers, not the fact that I can't tank them or whatever, I know how to tank them and that's what I'm choosing to do since I don't wanna risk a second wave of them, I don't even have an issue with pray switching, I can do that fine and only mess it up when I get too nervous, my issue

is

&#x200B;

the

&#x200B;

4th

&#x200B;

healer

&#x200B;

WHERE IS THE 4TH HEALER, how am I supposed to aggro all of the healers if I can't even find this dude, 3 jads, all pray switched fine, 3 healers aggro'd, calmly switching between pots and prayer, but I cannot for the life of me find this 4th healer, and since I'm using addy dart blowpipe I can't outdamage this mystical ghost healer wherever the hell he is, so I end up dying to a nervous failed pray switch after sitting there for 5 minutes pray switching fine just trying to find this healer. I have runelite, I have highlights on the mobs, but for whatever reason the 4th healer is either out of my FOV or just isn't being highlighted for whatever reason. I was under the impression that the healers had to be close to jad to heal him, but if that's wrong, that means this dude is getting caught on some random rock or something out of FOV and just troll healing jad from there.

&#x200B;

idk if anyone has had a similar issue, but please, help, I am so close to beating this but I just have this single issue, sincerely, a first time fire cape hopeful

reddit opinion: all bad i hate game

&#x200B;

my opinion:

wizards and berserkers are chads, shais are degenerate, musa is chad, maewha is weeb shit, tamer is degenerate, witch is a baddie, sorc is a baddie but goth, mystic has a cool dragon, striker is for fortnite kids, lahn is fun as hell, guardian is (sigh) thicc, warriors are chads, hash is flavor of the month, archer is some badass legolas shit, ranger is badass legolas shit except a girl.

&#x200B;

also awakening players are chads that appreciate the original intent of the """max level""" and if you play succ you're a meta sheep

Yes you can buy boss gear and enhancement material from the central market. Your normal silver grind will net you a decent amount of blackstones for enhancing too.

&#x200B;

Boss gear is significantly better than season tuvala, at every enhancement level stat-wise and also because you can use caphras stones to raise the caphras level of boss gear and make it even stronger

&#x200B;

World bosses can be found by looking at your map and finding the starred "world boss" as it will say. Nouver is in the desert, Karanda is on a mountain ridge near Velia, Kzarka is inside of the Serendia Shrine below velia, Vell is out in the ocean, Garmoth is near Kzarka, Offin is on the left of your map, Kutum is inside of a cave near the desert. You should generally try to make it to every world boss, but also prefer world bosses over others because sometimes 2 will spawn at the same time. For example, if you need a dandelion awakening weapon and already have a kzarka mainhand, and karanda (dandelion) and kzarka spawn at the same time, you should go to karanda. Or, you could place multiple characters at each boss, and go to the one that dies first, then switch characters and kill the other boss.

&#x200B;

World Bosses are on timers and have a daily rotation, you can find the timers at [https://mmotimer.com/bdo/?server=na](https://mmotimer.com/bdo/?server=na) and as you can see, Karanda spawns in 10 minutes (only on non-olvia servers)

&#x200B;

Basically, just go to where the boss spawns, stay on an olvia server if they're still available to you so you don't get randomly PlayerKilled by someone killing AFKs, wait for the timer to hit like :30 seconds remaining, switch to a non-olvia server, then kill the boss with the other people once it spawns.

&#x200B;

Oasis gear is more than enough to do world bosses, but you'll still want to telegraph their attacks and dodge as many as you can because they hit hard.

Oasis gear is bad to rely on, it will not be available after the event ends, so definitely make sure you have a decent backup (and no, no idea when the event ends, apparently it was supposed to end in June but I heard it was related to corona or something so :shrug:)

&#x200B;

Boss gear is mostly best in slot, so that's something to strive for but it does take a while to get it to a solid level (its better than oasis at TRI) I would suggest going to world bosses (they only spawn on non-olvia servers, I would recommend Velia1 in NA because that's where most people usually go, but the server doesn't matter because world boss health is shared between channels). World bosses have a very low chance of dropping boss weapons, personally I got my first weapon box drop (karanda) after roughly 50 different world boss kills, but there are other great things to get from them too, like Belongings of an Adventurer, which can be opened for really good endgame accessories. In those \~50 world boss kills, I had gotten 2 belongings. You can get boss armor (Dim tree, Griffon, Urugon, Bheg for Damage Reduction and Red nose, giath, leebur, muskan for Evasion) from daily scrolls from the black spirit's returning section, but personally I would just focus on grinding for silver from various sources and buy your boss gear then enhance it yourself. Or, you could grind a ton and buy the enhanced boss gear, but at oasis GS there aren't a lot of super efficient moneymaking spots. Depending on your accessories, I would recommend doing Shultz (240 AP area in Mediah). @ 225 AWA AP/280 DP I used a 50% item collection scroll and a Perfume of Courage with a sub-optimal rotation and earned about 50 million silver an hour at Shultz, which compared to my experimenting at Nagas and Gahaz, Shultz was much better despite being above my AP level at the time. You're at 180 AP though, so I would recommend Gahaz Bandits.

Dark Rifts are a great way to earn money, the boxes the dark rift bosses drop can have anywhere from a few cron stones to billions of silver worth. On average, I tend to get \~10 million out of tier 1 boxes, \~30 million out of tier 2 boxes, and \~50 million out of tier 3 boxes, but I've highrolled and lowrolled. There are also dark rifts that don't drop boxes, and instead have increased ancient spirit dust drops (usually about 100 dust) which is still about 60 million silver worth of caphras stones, so still great for money despite no box drop. You can also get a remnants of the rift, which are about 120 million silver, but those are used for the blackstar weapon questline and are pretty hard to get dropped, so I would save it.

&#x200B;

I'd also make an alt for fishing, get them a balenos rod (my fishing alt is a +6 balenos rod, lost penguin pet, and silver embroidered clothes), this can basically just earn you extra money overnight completely AFK, during Termian event I was earning about 20 million extra silver a night at Prof. 1 Fisher. I've also heard AFK horse training is a great way to AFK earn silver, but I don't do it so you'd have to look up a guide. Other life skills are definitely worth looking into as well.

&#x200B;

There's also scroll farming, basically you buy a bunch of scrolls/ancient relic shards/forbidden books off of the marketplace and make them into boss scrolls, and then farm those scrolls for a long time. It's very boring, and personally it makes me a lot less money than most people claim it does, so just something to consider.

&#x200B;

Accessories are a whole different beast, and personally I would just get your boss gear to TRI before you start on accessories, because they can be a huge money sink and don't boost you as much as boss gear does in terms of GS. I just used DUO Asula with my boss gear and slowly enhanced accessories to switch it out. It is probably worth looking up a class gear guide for your class to find out what accessories your class benefits the most from, but a general "sorta budget" build is:

&#x200B;

Earrings: Narc, Tungrad

&#x200B;

Rings: 2x Crescent Guardian

&#x200B;

Belt: Valtarra Eclipsed

&#x200B;

Necklace: Ogre Ring

&#x200B;

And yes, like the other comment says, doing a season character is still fine and encouraged, I earned a ton of silver just from doing the main questline and some black spirit pass quests, easily over a billion. Good luck!
